{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "98", "x": 0.9032117274603759, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03053152114325986, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "than \"idiot savants\" lacking the capacity to outwit us, even though they may", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.8259900604107785, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "greatly surpass us in the ability to calculate and process information.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.7105175377648104, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Wolpert's response was to say that we have already seen the damaging effects of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.1896453759080105, "w": 0.8263163973387393, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "artificial intelligence in the form of computer viruses. 'But in this case,' he says,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21797572598214812, "w": 0.826011898225939, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'the real intelligence is the malicious designer. Critically, the benefits of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24630607605628574, "w": 0.8265864480670612, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "computers outweigh the damage that computer viruses cause. Similarly, while", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2746735439806541, "w": 0.8262294561779128, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "there may be misuses of robotics in the near future, the benefits that they will", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3030039694975767, "w": 0.8260989419117193, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "bring are likely to outweigh these negative aspects.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33133430071101805, "w": 0.5340914182205092, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Richardson's response to this question was this: 'We need to ask why fears of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.36945418201235786, "w": 0.8262797959302309, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "artificial intelligence and robots persist; none have in fact risen up and challenged", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39778456980788796, "w": 0.8262947645734865, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "human supremacy.' She believes that as robots have never shown themselves to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4261149576034181, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "be a threat to humans, it seems unlikely that they ever will. In fact, she went on,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4544453076775557, "w": 0.8262391960485242, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'Not all fear [robots]; many people welcome machine intelligence.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.48280040298518045, "w": 0.6748392126780718, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "In answer to the fourth question, 'What can science fiction tell us about robotics?',", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5210686802446579, "w": 0.8263381326289458, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Rees replied, 'I sometimes advise students that it's better to read first-rate", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5493990303187956, "w": 0.8267884222260566, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "science fiction than second-rate science - more stimulating, and perhaps no more", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5777294181143257, "w": 0.8264938680337754, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "likely to be wrong.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6060597681884633, "w": 0.19682738068325295, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "As his response, Wolpert commented, 'Science fiction has often been remarkable", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6441796872111956, "w": 0.8263331089062095, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "at predicting the future Science fiction has painted a vivid spectrum of possible", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6725471551355638, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "futures, from cute and helpful robots to dystopian robotic societies. Interestingly,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7008775052097015, "w": 0.8265315972167756, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "almost no science fiction envisages a future without robots.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7292079307266242, "w": 0.6147707137059357, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finally, on the question of science fiction, Richardson pointed out that in modern", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7674761325433166, "w": 0.8267996999709751, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "society, people tend to think there is reality on the one hand, and fiction and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7958065580602393, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "fantasy on the other. She then explained that the division did not always exist, and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8241369081343769, "w": 0.8263600729690601, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that scientists and technologists made this separation because they wanted to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8524672582085145, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "carve out the sphere of their work. 'But the divide is not so clear cut, and that is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8806740330007866, "w": 0.8259453595309196, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "why the worlds seem to collide at times,' she said. 'In some cases, we need to bring", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9090043830749241, "w": 0.8261861906474072, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "these different understandings together to get a whole perspective. Perhaps", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9373348085918468, "w": 0.826077001571605, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}